      hook: `God appears to the ninety-nine-year-old Abram, renames him Abraham, establishes circumcision as the covenant sign, and promises a son by Sarah.`,
      tour: `Genesis 17 is the Priestly account of what chapter 15 accomplished in the Yahwist narrative: the formal establishment of the covenant with Abram. The two accounts are complementary rather than contradictory, and together they give the covenant both the intimate character of the night vision and the formal legal character of the Priestly covenant document. What is new here is the name change — Abram to Abraham, Sarai to Sarah — which in the ancient world indicated a change of identity and status, and the institution of circumcision as the sign of the covenant. God requires circumcision of every male in Abraham's household, including slaves, and specifies that any uncircumcised male will be cut off from his people, breaking the covenant. Then Abraham falls on his face and laughs at the promise of a son from a hundred-year-old man and a ninety-year-old woman, and asks that God bless Ishmael instead. God says no: the covenant is through Sarah's son, who will be called Isaac.`,
