      n: 18,
      title: "Genesis 18",
      tourTitle: "Three Visitors and the Plea for Sodom",
      hook: `Three men visit Abraham at Mamre; Sarah laughs at the promise of a son; Abraham bargains with God over the fate of the righteous in Sodom.`,
      tour: `Genesis 18 contains two distinct episodes of enormous theological weight. In the first, three men appear at Abraham's tent at Mamre and he receives them with extravagant hospitality — running to them, bowing, calling for water and a great feast, selecting the best calf. In the context of his time this kind of hospitality to strangers was not only a moral duty but the foundation of social order in a desert world. One of the visitors announces that Sarah will have a son in a year. Sarah, in the tent, hears this and laughs. God's response — why did Sarah laugh? Is anything too hard for the LORD? — is the chapter's theological center. Then the men set out toward Sodom and God pauses to tell Abraham what he is about to do, and Abraham's extraordinary bargaining prayer begins. Count the steps: fifty, forty-five, forty, thirty, twenty, ten. And God agrees each time. The chapter ends before we know whether ten righteous people are in Sodom.`,
