      title: "Genesis 25",
      tourTitle: "Abraham's Death and Esau and Jacob",
      hook: `Abraham dies full of years and is buried at Machpelah; Isaac's twin sons Esau and Jacob struggle in the womb, and Esau sells his birthright for stew.`,
      tour: `Genesis 25 is a transitional chapter that closes one generation and opens the next. Abraham's death at one hundred and seventy-five is understated — he dies full of years, satisfied — and the details of his burial by both Isaac and Ishmael signal that the two sons are at peace with each other even if the narrative has separated them. Then Ishmael's genealogy appears and closes, and the story shifts to Isaac and Rebekah, barren like Sarah before her, and Isaac's prayer. Rebekah conceives twins who struggle inside her; she goes to inquire of the LORD. God's oracle — two nations are in your womb, the elder shall serve the younger — is the chapter's pivot. Esau comes out first, red and hairy. Jacob comes out gripping Esau's heel. When they grow up, Esau, a hunter and his father's favorite, returns famished one day. Jacob is cooking red stew. Esau asks for some. Jacob requires, first, the birthright. Esau, who despised his birthright, agrees. The exchange sets up the conflict that will drive the next twelve chapters.`,
