      hook: `A blind old man, a bowl of stew, and a goatskin: Jacob steals Esau's blessing and sets the next twenty years in motion.`,
      tour: `Chapter 27 is the hinge on which Jacob's life turns. Isaac is old and his eyes are dim. He summons Esau, his preferred son, and tells him to hunt game, prepare a savory dish, and receive the paternal blessing. Rebekah overhears, sends Jacob to get two goat kids, dresses Jacob in Esau's clothes and the skins of the kids to simulate his brother's hairy arms, and sends him in first. The scene is excruciating: Isaac asks directly, Are you really Esau? The voice is Jacob's voice, but the hands are Esau's hands. Isaac blesses Jacob with the dew of heaven, the fat of the earth, dominion over his brothers, and the curse that falls on any who curse him. Esau returns, the deception is discovered, Isaac trembles, Esau weeps and asks for any remaining blessing. He gets thorns and exile. He begins to hate Jacob and plans to kill him after their father dies. Rebekah sends Jacob away to Haran before blood is shed.`,
