      title: "Genesis 28",
      tourTitle: "Jacob's ladder at Bethel",
      hook: `A fugitive lies down at a stone pillow and wakes into the first great theophany of his life: a stairway to heaven and a renewed promise.`,
      tour: `Genesis 28 opens with Isaac formally blessing Jacob for the journey to Paddan-aram and instructing him not to marry a Canaanite woman. Jacob sets out alone — he arrives at Bethel at nightfall, takes a stone for a pillow, and dreams. The dream is one of the most arresting images in the Bible: a ladder or stairway set on the earth with its top reaching to heaven, and the angels of God ascending and descending on it, and the Lord standing above it. God speaks the full Abrahamic covenant directly to Jacob: land, descendants as the dust of the earth, blessing for all the families of the earth. Jacob wakes afraid — how awesome is this place, he says; this is none other than the house of God and the gate of heaven. He sets the stone upright as a pillar, pours oil on it, names the place Bethel (house of God), and makes a conditional vow: if God is with me on this journey and brings me back safely, then the Lord will be my God. The vow is honest — it is the bargaining of a man not yet sure, not the settled faith of Abraham.`,
