      tourTitle: "Jacob meets Rachel; Leah's wedding trick",
      hook: `The deceiver is deceived: Jacob works seven years for Rachel and wakes beside Leah, matched deception for deception.`,
      tour: `Jacob arrives at a well in the east and meets Rachel watering her father's sheep. He rolls away the stone single-handedly, kisses her, and weeps with relief. He is brought to Laban's house, works a month, and negotiates: seven years of service for Rachel's hand. The seven years seem like a few days, the text says, because of his love for her. At the feast Laban substitutes Leah, the older daughter, under the bridal veil. In the morning Jacob discovers the switch. Laban defends himself: in our place the younger is not given before the firstborn. The irony is precise — the man who exploited the convention of firstborn blessing to rob his older brother is now on the receiving end of a first-born-first convention. He can have Rachel for another seven years of service. He marries her the following week. The chapter ends with the fertile-barren reversal: God sees that Leah is unloved and opens her womb; Rachel is loved and barren. Leah bears Reuben, Simeon, Levi, and Judah — the last named because she says she will praise the Lord. Then she stops bearing.`,
