      title: "Genesis 34",
      tourTitle: "The rape of Dinah and Shechem's revenge",
      hook: `A Hivite prince violates Dinah and then proposes marriage; Simeon and Levi accept under false terms and massacre a city.`,
      tour: `Chapter 34 is one of the most disturbing chapters in Genesis and one of the most carefully constructed. Dinah, Jacob's daughter by Leah, goes out to visit the women of the land. Shechem son of Hamor the Hivite sees her, takes her, lies with her, and violates her — the text is clinical and quick. Then the text says he loves her and speaks tenderly to her, and asks his father to get her for a wife. Hamor approaches Jacob to negotiate the match; Jacob's sons, when they hear, are angry and grieve. They respond with a condition: all the men of Shechem must be circumcised and then intermarriage can proceed. Hamor and Shechem persuade their city; the men comply. On the third day, while the men are still in pain, Simeon and Levi take their swords and kill every male in the city. They take Dinah from Shechem's house and leave. Jacob is appalled — you have troubled me and made me stink among the inhabitants of the land. Simeon and Levi answer with a question the narrative leaves standing: should he have treated our sister as a harlot?`,
