      title: "Genesis 35",
      tourTitle: "Bethel, Rachel's death, Isaac's death",
      hook: `Jacob returns to Bethel as promised, buries Rachel on the road to Ephrath, and watches his father Isaac die at last in Hebron.`,
      tour: `Chapter 35 closes the cycle of Jacob's return with a series of deaths and renaming. God tells Jacob to go up to Bethel, build an altar, and fulfill the vow he made when he fled from Esau. Jacob orders his household to put away foreign gods and purify themselves; they give him all the rings and earrings and foreign gods, and he buries them under the oak at Shechem. At Bethel God appears again, repeats the name Israel, and speaks the Abrahamic covenant for the last time in Genesis in its full form: be fruitful and multiply, a nation and a company of nations shall come from you, and kings. God goes up and Jacob sets a pillar and pours oil on it. Then the journey south: Rachel goes into labor near Bethlehem and dies bearing Benjamin. Jacob buries her by the road — the only patriarch not buried at Machpelah. Reuben sleeps with Bilhah, Jacob's concubine; Jacob hears and says nothing, but the offense will be named again in chapter 49. The twelve sons are listed. Isaac dies at Hebron at one hundred and eighty; Esau and Jacob bury him together.`,
