      title: "Genesis 43",
      tourTitle: "The brothers return with Benjamin",
      hook: `Judah gives himself as surety for Benjamin and Jacob relents; the brothers return to Egypt and are invited to Joseph's table — and still don't know who he is.`,
      tour: `The famine continues and the grain from Egypt runs out. Jacob tells his sons to go back and buy more. Judah reminds him of the Egyptian lord's condition — they cannot go without Benjamin. He makes a formal guarantee: if I do not bring him back, let me bear the blame before you forever. Jacob relents, tells them to take double the silver and the best products of the land — balm, honey, gum, myrrh, pistachio nuts, almonds — as a gift. The brothers arrive; Joseph sees Benjamin and orders that they dine at his house. They are afraid, suspecting the returned silver will be used against them. They explain to Joseph's steward; he reassures them — your God and the God of your father gave you treasure in your sacks; I received your silver. At the dinner, Joseph is served separately, the brothers are served separately, and the Egyptians eat separately (they could not eat with Hebrews, the text notes — the first reference to this cultural boundary in Genesis). Joseph orders their portions brought from his own table, and Benjamin's portion is five times larger than the others. They drink and are merry with him.`,
