      title: "Genesis 44",
      tourTitle: "The silver cup and Judah's plea",
      hook: `Joseph plants his silver cup in Benjamin's sack — and Judah's response shows that something real has changed in the man who sold his brother.`,
      tour: `Joseph plants his silver divination cup in Benjamin's sack alongside the returned silver and sends the brothers on their way, then sends his steward after them to accuse them of theft. They are horrified — we swore we did not steal; let the one with the cup die. The steward searches and finds the cup in Benjamin's sack. They tear their garments, return to the city, fall before Joseph. Joseph questions them: did you not know that a man like me can divine? Judah speaks for all. What can we say? God has found out the guilt of your servants. They will all be his slaves. Joseph insists: only Benjamin. The rest go free. Judah comes forward and delivers what is, structurally, the key speech of the Joseph novella: he recounts the whole sequence of events — the old father who loves this son of his old age, the dead brother, the warning that losing Benjamin would bring Jacob's gray hair down to Sheol in sorrow — and ends with an offer: let me stay as Joseph's slave in Benjamin's place. Let the boy go home with his brothers.`,
